Automate sdmx-dl from a single Java script using jbang, leveraging the Java API without Maven/Gradle setup.
A simple jbang Java script that uses the sdmx-dl API to print the last 12 observations as a CSV table:
//usr/bin/env jbang &#34;$0&#34; &#34;$@&#34; ; exit $? //JAVA 25+ //DEPS com.github.nbbrd.sdmx-dl:sdmx-dl-standalone:3.2.0 import sdmxdl.DataRequest; import sdmxdl.web.SdmxWebManager; void main() throws Exception { var data = SdmxWebManager.ofServiceLoader() .usingName(&#34;ECB&#34;) .getData(DataRequest.builder() .flowOf(&#34;EXR&#34;) .keyOf(&#34;M.CHF.EUR.SP00.A&#34;) .lastNObservations(12) .build()); IO.println(&#34;Series,ObsPeriod,ObsValue&#34;); data.forEach(series -&gt; series.getObs().forEach(obs -&gt; IO.println(series.getKey() + &#34;,&#34; + obs.getPeriod().getStart() + &#34;,&#34; + obs.getValue()))); } Save as FetchSdmx.java and run:
